(Most Recently Used) ===</strong><br>Evict the page used most recently.<br><code>7</code> F → [7] · <code>0</code> F → [7, 0] · <code>1</code> F → [7, 0, 1]<br><code>2</code> F, evict 1 (most recent) → [7, 0, 2]<br><code>0</code> <strong>HIT</strong> (0 is now most recent)<br><code>3</code> F, evict 0 → [7, 2, 3]<br><code>0</code> F, evict 3 → [7, 2, 0]<br><code>4</code> F, evict 0 → [7, 2, 4]<br><code>2</code> <strong>HIT</strong><br><code>3</code> F, evict 2 → [7, 4, 3]<br><code>0</code> F, evict 3 → [7, 4, 0]<br><code>3</code> F, evict 0 → [7, 4, 3]<br><code>2</code> F, evict 3 → [7, 4, 2]<br><strong>MRU page faults = 11</strong> (hits = 2)<br><br><strong>=== FINAL COMPARISON on this string, 3 frames ===</strong><br>Optimal = <strong>7</strong> faults (best possible)<br>LRU = <strong>9</strong> faults<br>FIFO = <strong>10</strong> faults (from the previous topic)<br>MRU = <strong>11</strong> faults (worst here)<br><br>LRU comes closest to Optimal — which is exactly why real operating systems try to approximate LRU.",
